d-limits","4.reference\u002F1.types-and-limits",{"title":70,"path":71,"stem":72},"Splitting and compile","\u002Freference\u002Fsplitting-and-compile","4.reference\u002F2.splitting-and-compile",{"title":74,"path":75,"stem":76},"State and metrics","\u002Freference\u002Fstate-and-metrics","4.reference\u002F3.state-and-metrics",{"title":78,"path":79,"stem":80},"Composables","\u002Freference\u002Fcomposables","4.reference\u002F4.composables",{"title":82,"path":83,"stem":84},"Components","\u002Freference\u002Fcomponents","4.reference\u002F5.components",{"id":86,"title":36,"body":87,"description":182,"extension":183,"links":184,"meta":185,"navigation":186,"path":37,"seo":187,"stem":38,"__hash__":188},"docs\u002F2.using-the-tool\u002F4.text-tools.md",{"type":88,"value":89,"toc":175},"minimark",[90,94,98,103,115,119,154,158,172],[91,92,36],"h1",{"id":93},"text-tools",[95,96,97],"p",{},"Three switches sit under the marker fields. Each one has an icon. They replace the old \"Flatten blank lines\" control, which did not change the packed posts: a blank line was already treated as a space.",[99,100,102],"h2",{"id":101},"capitalize-posts","Capitalize posts",[95,104,105,106,110,111,114],{},"The first visible letter of each post becomes uppercase. The chunks are not packed again, so the order stays. ",[107,108,109],"code",{},"alpha beta"," is published as ",[107,112,113],{},"Alpha beta",".",[99,116,118],{"id":117},"finish-sentences","Finish sentences",[95,120,121,122,124,125,124,128,124,131,134,135,138,139,141,142,145,146,149,150,153],{},"If a post does not already end with ",[107,123,114],{},", ",[107,126,127],{},"!",[107,129,130],{},"?",[107,132,133],{},"…",", or ",[107,136,137],{},"...",", the page adds ",[107,140,133],{},". ",[107,143,144],{},"Hello."," is left alone. ",[107,147,148],{},"Hello"," becomes ",[107,151,152],{},"Hello…",". The extra character is part of the published length, so the ring can move.",[99,155,157],{"id":156},"keep-line-breaks","Keep line breaks",[95,159,160,161,164,165,168,169,114],{},"Off, which is the default, a line break is just another space. ",[107,162,163],{},"hello"," and ",[107,166,167],{},"world"," on two lines become ",[107,170,171],{},"hello world",[95,173,174],{},"On, a line break stays in the post, and a blank line stays a blank line. Turning this on packs the source again and drops a hand-made order, because the shape of the chunks can change.",{"title":176,"searchDepth":177,"depth":177,"links":178},"",2,[179,180,181],{"id":101,"depth":177,"text":102},{"id":117,"depth":177,"text":118},{"id":156,"depth":177,"text":157},"Capitalize posts, finish sentences, and keep line breaks.","md",null,{},true,{"title":36,"description":182},"SbAsFMcuzHAUPjPitzYcaRG-vW8DWa7lgSrhX0Zr5FQ",[190,192],{"title":32,"path":33,"stem":34,"description":191,"children":-1},"How counters and the custom bridge are written into each post.",{"title":40,"path":41,"stem":42,"description":193,"children":-1},"Copy, download, listen, and send.",1792868107742]